  "query_preview": "..\n\nA weaker wave will move north from Haida Gwaii Tuesday and\nWednesday, providing enough disturbance to generate scattered\nshowers, mostly in the southern panhandle. The larger impacts may\ncome as early as Thursday from a much deeper low. The latter low \nwill intensify in the western Gulf, and will have ample to mature\nas it looks to be held out over the open waters of the Gulf by\nsome Fujiwara Effect related to a smaller orbiting low which most\nguidance has combining together.\n\nBy Friday the extent of its influence will likely reach us here \nin SEAK. Exact timing still differs between deterministic guidance\nruns. One of the larger variables being how long the two lows \norbit one another before joining and allowing the resultant low to\ntrack east. A later arrival will most likely result in a stronger\nsystem, but there is good confidence in strong gusty winds,\nespecially over coastal waters, and widespread rainfall Friday\nheading into the weekend.",
